    {
      "id": "claim_4f1a09bee1714903a527467479f9c63e",
      "statement": "The wallet revision counter distinguishes a reconnect of the same address from the address's previous session: it changes on every connect, switch, and disconnect, and all consumers gate work on the address+revision pair together (sameWallet in both widget syncs, walletIsCurrent in the background task), so reconnecting the same address cannot reuse the previous session's cached snapshots or let their in-flight requests win.",
